Local stability boundary of the administrative price-adjustment rule $u_{t+1}=u_t-g\,u_{t-k}$ (Proposition 1). For each information lag $k$ the critical gain is $g^\star(k)=2\sin[\pi/(2(2k+1))]$, attained at a conjugate pair of roots on the unit circle with argument $\theta_0=\pi/(2k+1)$, so the oscillation at the boundary has period $2(2k+1)$ quarters (Corollary 1). The penultimate column gives the large-$k$ asymptote $\pi/(2k+1)$ and the last column its ratio to the exact value.